{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNCaNxhDR8u3xSxS6ahc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The merger can now request a conflict round, and review-fix records and handles the round's reason. The feature is off in production. `servecmd` leaves the merger's `Rounds` dependency unset, so a conflicting PR still goes to `needs-human`. `go test ./...`, `go vet ./...` and `gofmt` all pass, and the existing tests pass unchanged.\n\n- **Review-fix:**\n  - A conflict round lands when the PR head is a merge commit that has the round's head as an ancestor. Review rounds still land by the no-code check.\n  - If the head isn't such a merge, the round caps with reason conflict and its own comment wording.\n  - I added `IsAncestor` and `Parents` to `gitx` for this.\n- **Merger:** a new `conflict(...)` replaces both `needs-human` conflict calls (gate g and `updateBranch`). With a nil `Rounds`, an unparsable worker branch or an unconfigured worker role, it falls back to `needs-human`. It skips a head that already has a requested round, leaves a capped head to a human, and in dry run only logs.\n- **Cap and wording:**\n  - Conflict and review rounds share `max_review_rounds`, so \"counted separately\" is read as the reason being recorded on each round event. That is how the plan read it, and I followed it.\n  - A conflict cap comment lists all requested reviewer roles, because the merger passes them all. This is wording only.\n- **Docs:** `docs/proposal.md` and the merger and reviewfix package docs describe the request path and that it is off until part B.\n- **Tests:**\n  - The new tests are in `internal/merger/conflict_test.go`, `internal/reviewfix/loop_test.go` and `internal/gitx/gitx_test.go`.\n  - They cover the switch off and on, the shared cap with the real reviewfix loop, and the merge-head, plain-commit and unmoved-head landing cases.\n  - The pull request body is in `.ard/322/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":899,"cache_read_input_tokens":70468,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":899},"output_tokens":663,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dfccf11-15eb-4385-96da-9b8dce3becc5","uuid":"5693afff-2fbd-4ee4-9470-89b565858503","timestamp":"2026-11-24T18:08:41.359Z","request_id":"req_011ChNCaNoWm93xVz62vjdEU"}
